  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO1_UserAccess_Q01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why are permissions granted to a GROUP rather than to each user account?
  choices:
  - Windows does not allow permissions on individual accounts
  - Group permissions are processed faster
  - Groups use less disk space in the directory
  - Access follows the group, so adding or removing a person is one change
  correctChoiceIndex: 3
  points: 10
  explanation: When a student leaves you remove them from the group once, and every
    permission the group holds goes with them. Per-user permissions have to be hunted
    down one folder at a time.
